            <ArticleTitle>Aspirin and salicylate in respiratory disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>195-205</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4193/Rhino12.144</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article describes the natural history, pathogenesis and diagnosis of Aspirin Exacerbated Respiratory Disease. The evidence base for the role of oral aspirin and nasal L-Lysine-aspirin desensitisation is reviewed. Evidence for the role of dietary salicylic acid and its avoidance is also reviewed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
